.Dd April 30, 2026
.Dt EMULATION 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emulation
.Nd FreeBSD kernel emulation framework
.Sh SYNOPSIS
The
.Fx
emulation framework is provided by the following loadable kernel modules:
.Bl -tag -width "emu_core.ko" -compact
.It Pa emu_core.ko
Core emulation framework
.It Pa emu_amd64.ko
AMD64 architecture support
.It Pa emu_i386.ko
i386 architecture support
.It Pa emu_arm64.ko
ARM64 architecture support
.It Pa emu_arm.ko
ARM architecture support
.It Pa emu_powerpc.ko
PowerPC architecture support
.It Pa emu_riscv.ko
RISC-V architecture support
.It Pa emu.ko
Master module (loads all above)
.El
.Pp
To load all emulation modules:
.Dl "kldload emu"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fx
emulation framework provides a unified mechanism for running
emulated instances of different architectures on a
.Fx
host.
It supports both native virtualization via
.Xr bhyve 4
and pure software emulation for cross-architecture testing.
.Pp
The framework consists of:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Kernel Module
.Pa emu_core.ko
provides the core framework including instance management, sysctl
interface, and resource limits.
.It Per-Architecture Modules
.Pa emu_<arch>.ko
modules provide architecture-specific emulation support.
.It Userland Tool
.Xr emu 8
provides the command-line interface for managing emulated instances.
.El
.Ss Instance Lifecycle
An emulated instance goes through the following states:
.Bl -tag -width "INITIALIZING" -compact
.It INITIALIZING
Instance is being created
.It STOPPED
Instance exists but is not running
.It RUNNING
Instance is actively executing
.It PAUSED
Instance execution is paused
.It ERROR
Instance encountered an error
.El
.Ss Supported Architectures
The framework supports the following guest architectures:
.Bl -tag -width "amd64" -compact
.It amd64
x86-64 (64-bit)
.It i386
x86 (32-bit)
.It arm64
AArch64 (64-bit ARM)
.It arm
ARM (32-bit)
.It powerpc
PowerPC
.It riscv
RISC-V (64-bit)
.El
.Ss Execution Modes
.Bl -tag -width "EMU_MODE_EMULATOR" -compact
.It EMU_MODE_AUTO
Automatically select best mode based on architecture (default)
.It EMU_MODE_BHYVE
Use bhyve/VMM virtualization (native architectures only)
.It EMU_MODE_EMULATOR
Use custom software emulator (all architectures)
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following sysctl variables are available under the
.Va kern.emulation
tree:
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Va kern.emulation.allow_nonroot
.Pq Li int
Allow non-root users in the emu group to create and manage emulation
instances.
Default is 0 (root only).
Writable only by root.
.It Va kern.emulation.modules_loaded
.Pq Li string
Comma-separated list of currently loaded emulation modules.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.instance_count
.Pq Li int
Total number of emulated instances.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.max_instances
.Pq Li int
Maximum concurrent emulated instances allowed.
Default is 16.
.It Va kern.emulation.max_memory_per_instance
.Pq Li int
Maximum memory per instance in megabytes.
Default is 4096.
.It Va kern.emulation.max_instances_per_user
.Pq Li int
Maximum instances per non-root user.
Default is 4.
.It Va kern.emulation.max_memory_per_user
.Pq Li int
Maximum total memory for all instances per user in megabytes.
Default is 4096.
.It Va kern.emulation.max_cpu_time_per_instance
.Pq Li int
Maximum CPU time per instance in seconds (0 = unlimited).
Default is 0.
.It Va kern.emulation.sandbox_capsicum
.Pq Li int
Enable Capsicum sandboxing for emulator processes (default: 1).
.It Va kern.emulation.sandbox_strict
.Pq Li int
Fail instance creation if Capsicum is unavailable (default: 0).
.It Va kern.emulation.drop_privileges
.Pq Li int
Drop root privileges after setup (default: 1).
.It Va kern.emulation.watchdog_seconds
.Pq Li int
Default watchdog timeout in seconds.
Default is 30.
.It Va kern.emulation.securelevel_restrictions
.Pq Li int
Enable securelevel-aware operation restrictions (default: 1).
.El
.Ss Memory Management Sysctls
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.policy
.Pq Li string
Memory allocation policy:
.Bl -tag -width "demand" -compact
.It prealloc
Pre-allocate all guest memory (default)
.It demand
Use demand paging with mmap(MAP_NORESERVE)
.El
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.overcommit
.Pq Li int
Allow memory overcommit (0=disabled, 1=warn, 2=silent).
Default is 0 (disabled).
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.warn_percent
.Pq Li int
Warn when configured memory exceeds this percentage of available host RAM.
Default is 80.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.balloon_min_pct
.Pq Li int
Minimum balloon size as percentage of allocated memory.
Default is 50.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.balloon_interval
.Pq Li int
Balloon adjustment interval in seconds.
Default is 30.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.system_reserve_percent
.Pq Li int
Percentage of total physical memory reserved for system use.
Default is 10.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.total
.Pq Li int
Total physical memory in bytes.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.system_used
.Pq Li int
System-wide used memory in bytes.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.available
.Pq Li int
Available memory for emulation in bytes.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.instances_used
.Pq Li int
Total memory used by all emulation instances in bytes.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.scrub.enabled
.Pq Li int
Enable memory scrubbing on instance destroy (default: 1).
.It Va kern.emulation.memory.scrub.method
.Pq Li string
Memory scrubbing method:
.Bl -tag -width "zero" -compact
.It zero
Fill with zeros (default)
.It random
Fill with random data
.It pattern
Fill with configurable pattern
.El
.El
.Ss Audit Sysctls
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.enabled
.Pq Li int
Enable audit logging (default: 1).
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.destination
.Pq Li int
Audit log destination (0=none, 1=syslog, 2=file, 3=both).
Default is 1.
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.file
.Pq Li string
Audit log file path.
Default is
.Pa /var/log/emu_audit.log .
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.rotation_size
.Pq Li int
Audit log rotation size in bytes.
Default is 10485760 (10MB).
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.rotation_count
.Pq Li int
Number of rotated log files to keep.
Default is 5.
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.min_severity
.Pq Li int
Minimum severity level to log (0=EMERG, 7=DEBUG).
Default is 6 (INFO).
.It Va kern.emulation.audit.event_count
.Pq Li int
Total number of audit events logged.
Read-only.
.El
.Ss Per-Module Sysctls
For each loaded module, the following sysctls are available under
.Va kern.emulation.module.<name> :
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Va kern.emulation.module.<name>.version
.Pq Li int
Module version number.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.module.<name>.refcount
.Pq Li int
Current reference count (number of instances using this module).
Read-only.
.El
.Ss Instance Sysctls
For each instance, the following sysctls are available under
.Va kern.emulation.instance.<name> :
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Va kern.emulation.instance.<name>.state
.Pq Li string
Instance state (stopped, running, paused, error).
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.instance.<name>.arch
.Pq Li string
Target architecture.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.instance.<name>.memory_used
.Pq Li int
Current memory usage in bytes.
Read-only.
.It Va kern.emulation.instance.<name>.cpu_time
.Pq Li int
Total CPU time used in nanoseconds.
Read-only.
.El
.Sh KERNEL OPTIONS
The following kernel options enable the emulation framework build:
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Va MK_EMULATION
Build the emulation framework (default: no).
When enabled, builds:
.Bl -tag -width "emu.8" -compact
.It Kernel modules in
.Pa sys/modules/emu*/
.It Userland tool
.Pa usr.sbin/emu/
.It Man pages
.Pa usr.sbin/emu/emu.8 ,
.Pa usr.sbin/emu/emu.conf.5 ,
.Pa sys/emulation/emulation.4
.El
.It Va MK_TESTS
Build the emulation framework test suite (default: no).
Requires
.Va MK_EMULATION .
.El
.Sh LOADING
The emulation framework modules can be loaded individually or as a complete set:
.Bl -tag -width "kldload emu" -compact
.It Li "kldload emu_core"
Load only the core framework
.It Li "kldload emu_amd64"
Load AMD64 support
.It Li "kldload emu"
Load master module (loads all modules in correct dependency order)
.El
.Pp
To unload, use
.Xr kldunload 8 :
.Dl "kldunload emu"
.Pp
Note: Modules cannot be unloaded while instances are running.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "kern.emulation" -compact
.It Va /var/emu/
Default instance data directory
.It Va /var/emu/instances/
Per-instance data directories
.It Va /var/cache/emu/images/
Disk image cache
.It Va /var/log/emu_audit.log
Default audit log location
.It Va /boot/kernel/emu*.ko
Kernel modules
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xr emu 8
Userland management tool
.It Xr emu.conf 5
Configuration file
.It Xr bhyve 4
Native virtualization
.It Xr vmm 4
Virtual Machine Monitor
.It Xr kldload 8
Load kernel modules
.It Xr kldunload 8
Unload kernel modules
.El
.Sh HISTORY
The emulation framework first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
